Z||000009||K9||09-04-99||04:32 PM||||Check out the Fiero Store!!!<br>
Z||000010||DXR_DAD||09-04-99||06:18 PM||||Bruce what is the flow master part no.  At one time I asked a muffler shop and they said flower doesn`t make a muffler for the fiero. I thought it was a firebird dual outlet that would if with some modifications. What is the case size on that 80.  Let me know when you install. What type of piping?
Z||000011||Bruce||09-04-99||07:39 PM||||Bill, <br>The part number is: 42583. Hopefully, no serious modifications have to be made to accomodate it.<br>The general plan is to install upgraded stock-type manifolds from Ed Parks, add the flowmaster and a high flow cat. converter, and use 2 1/4 pipe to the cat. and 2 1/2 from there to the muffler. As always, I'm following along with the advice I've been reading through the forum. So far, so good.<br>What do you think, and can your buddy help me with the installation?<br>bruce
Z||000012||DXR_DAD||09-04-99||07:55 PM||||Bruce I can help with this, catch me on E-Mail. My muffler and cat. was done by a shop in Daly City.
Z||000013||batboy||09-11-1999||09:40 AM||||Bruce, sorry it took me so long to respond, but I don't know anything about the 80 series muffler. My JEGS catalog doesn't list the dimensions for those mufflers. A good shop can make almost anything fit though.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Gokart||09-11-1999||07:49 PM||||Recently changed my entire exhaust system. Went with the Fiero Stores Gorlic stock exhaust system for 179.00 and a new cat can for 119.00 and had Midas put it on for 90.00. I'm happy with it and didn't notice any lack of power.||||reg||14
